// ArgoUML, application module (argouml-app, 1,237 classes in 77 packages), context declared from the developers'
// Cookbook as migrated into the project wiki (chapters 4 "ArgoUML Design, The Big Picture" and 5 "Inside the
// subsystems"), by someone who did not write the program. The wiki's own words are quoted in the comments.
//
// Layers, bottom to top:
//   Low-level subsystems: "infrastructure subsystems that just are there for every other subsystem to use - but
//     they are not using any other part of ArgoUML": Internationalization, TaskManagement, Configuration,
//     Swing extensions, The Model ("Everything within ArgoUML should access the Model subsystem through the
//     interfaces in the org.argouml.model package").
//   View and Control subsystems: Diagrams, GUI, Property panels, Explorer, Notation, Code Generation, Reverse
//     Engineering, Module loader, Persistence, Profile ("rely on the information in the model subsystems").
//     The GUI "has no knowledge of UML, Critics, Diagrams, or Model"; "the persistence subsystem depends on the
//     kernel subsystem, and not vice versa".
//   Loadable subsystems: Critics and checklists, OCL, the languages ("connected only through the interfaces
//     provided by other subsystems", "enabled and disabled using the module loader").
//   Top level: Application ("depends on other ArgoUML subsystems, but no other ArgoUML subsystem depends on the
//     top level").
axis lowlevel    = [org.argouml.i18n, org.argouml.taskmgmt, org.argouml.configuration, org.argouml.swingext,
                    org.argouml.util]
axis model       = [org.argouml.model]
axis kernel      = [org.argouml.kernel]
axis gui         = [org.argouml.ui, org.argouml.gefext, org.argouml.language.ui]
axis diagrams    = [org.argouml.uml.diagram]
axis panels      = [org.argouml.uml.ui]
axis uml         = [org.argouml.uml, org.argouml.uml.util]
axis notation    = [org.argouml.notation]
axis codegen     = [org.argouml.uml.generator]
axis reveng      = [org.argouml.uml.reveng]
axis persistence = [org.argouml.persistence]
axis profile     = [org.argouml.profile]
axis modules     = [org.argouml.moduleloader]
axis cognitive   = [org.argouml.cognitive, org.argouml.uml.cognitive, org.argouml.pattern.cognitive.critics]
axis ocl         = [org.argouml.ocl]
axis application = [org.argouml.application]

// The documented order: the low-level layer changes least (nothing of ArgoUML below it), then the model and the
// kernel, then the view-and-control subsystems, unordered among themselves, then the loadable ones, which only
// use the others, then the application, which "no other ArgoUML subsystem depends on".
speed lowlevel < model < kernel < gui, diagrams, panels, uml, notation, codegen, reveng, persistence, profile, modules
      < cognitive, ocl < application;

// Decisions written in the documentation: the GUI knows nothing of the model, the diagrams, UML or the critics.
hide model, diagrams, uml, panels, cognitive from gui;
friend tests of all;

// BEGIN optional: the view-and-control subsystems kept apart from one another (ADP), which the documentation does
// not state; the Diagrams page lists the GUI and Notation among the subsystems it uses, so this block will report
// those uses as well.
apart gui, diagrams, panels, uml, notation, codegen, reveng, persistence, profile, modules;
// END optional
